# Maps program — private repository (owner, 2026-09-29: "upload this all to a github repository").
# Kept LOCAL ONLY, and why:
#  - captures/              2.5 GB of recorded sessions of the reference generators, including their program bundles
#                            (third-party code; the clean-room rule forbids handing it to implementers) and session logs
#  - reference/             third-party source repositories (TownGeneratorOS, a Foundry module) with their own .git
#  - research/patreon/      995 MB archive of watabou's Patreon posts (third-party, copyrighted)
#  - research/devlogs/      itch.io devlog copies (third-party)
#  - research/ftg-docs/     copies of the Fantasy Town Generator's guide pages (third-party)
#  - research/external/     fetched third-party pages
#  - research/reference-maps/ copyrighted study images (Wizards of the Coast, Larian)
#  - profiler/.profiles/    browser profiles used for capture (may hold site logins)
#  - profiler/node_modules/ installable dependencies (npm install restores them)
#  - backups/               local snapshot tarballs (git history replaces them)
captures/
reference/
research/patreon/
research/devlogs/
research/ftg-docs/
research/external/
research/reference-maps/
profiler/.profiles/
profiler/node_modules/
backups/
.claude/
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
*.lock
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# live-run registration written by tools/lanes.py (session-local journal path)
docs/ACTIVE-RUN.json
